& =\frac{\mathrm{iA}}{\mathrm{mvr}}=\frac{\left(\frac{\mathrm{e} \omega}{2 \pi}\right)\left(\pi \mathrm{r}^2\right)}{\mathrm{m}(\mathrm{r} \omega) \mathrm{r}}=\frac{\mathrm{e}}{2 \mathrm{~m}}
\end{aligned}

It is independent of the orbit of the electron

